        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2b5ef3d2-0090-5c48-9a8b-a570082664ae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bo Diddley, Eric Clapton\n- Bands: The Yardbirds, the Beatles, the Rolling Stones, the Who, The Clash, Buddy Holly, Elvis Presley, Jimi Hendrix, George Thorogood, Parliament-Funkadelic\n- Songs: \"Before You Accuse Me\"\n- Albums: Journeyman\n- Places: London\n- Topics: rock and roll, blues, R&B, sobriety, alcohol addiction\n\nFacts:\n- Bo Diddley was born as Ellas Otha Bates on December 30, 1928, and he later became known professionally as Bo Diddley.\n- In 1957, Bo Diddley wrote and recorded the song \"Before You Accuse Me,\" which is also known as \"Before You Accuse Me (Take a Look at Yourself).\"\n- The Yardbirds formed in London in 1963 as an English rock band.\n- Bo Diddley was an American R&B singer, guitarist, songwriter, and music producer who played a key role in the transition from the blues to rock and roll.\n- Bo Diddley influenced artists including Elvis Presley, Buddy Holly, the Beatles, the Rolling Stones, the Yardbirds, Eric Clapton, the Who, Jimi Hendrix, George Thorogood, Parliament-Funkadelic, and The Clash.\n- Journeyman was heralded as a return to form for Eric Clapton after his struggles with alcohol addiction and his recent sobriety.\n- Journeyman has a 1980s electronic sound, but it also includes blues songs such as \"Before You Accuse Me,\" \"Running on Faith,\" and \"Hard Times.\"\n- Bo Diddley died on June 2, 2008.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "bef0b81b-bbf4-5717-aa19-6d14eed2e539",
        "text": "Page: Bo Diddley. Sentence: Ellas McDaniel (born Ellas Otha Bates, December 30, 1928 – June 2, 2008), known as Bo Diddley, was an American R&B singer, guitarist, songwriter and music producer who played a key role in the transition from the blues to rock and roll, and influenced artists including Elvis Presley, Buddy Holly, the Beatles, the Rolling Stones, the Yardbirds, Eric Clapton, the Who, Jimi Hendrix, George Thorogood, Parliament-Funkadelic, and The Clash.\nPage: The Yardbirds. Sentence: The Yardbirds are an English rock band, formed in London in 1963.\nPage: Before You Accuse Me. Sentence: \"Before You Accuse Me\" (also known as \"Before You Accuse Me (Take a Look at Yourself)\" is a song written and recorded by American musician Bo Diddley in 1957.\nPage: Journeyman (album). Sentence: Heralded as a return to form for Clapton, who had struggled with alcohol addiction and had recently found sobriety, the album has a 1980s electronic sound, but it also includes blues songs like \"Before You Accuse Me,\" \"Running on Faith,\" and \"Hard Times.\" \"",
